Hello QA,

During the final visual inspection of Metformin HCl API batch MET-26-0457 at the
packing line this morning, our inspector found glass-like particles in 3 of the
42 lined HDPE drums. The particles are 0.5-2 mm, clear, and were found on top of
the powder in drums 7, 19 and 34.

Deviation Reference: DEV-2026-131
Product: Metformin HCl API
Batch: MET-26-0457
Manufacturing Stage: Final blending and drum loading
Equipment or Area: Vibratory sieve S-201 and drum loader DL-03, Suite C
Incident Date: 2026-10-20
Reported By: Maria Lopez
Severity Suggested: Critical
Detected By: QC inspector during 100 % visual inspection at packing
Quantity Affected: 3 drums of 42 (150 kg)
Immediate Containment: All 42 drums of batch MET-26-0457 quarantined; Suite C
packing line stopped; sieve S-201 and loader DL-03 taken out of use.

What we have checked so far:

- The batch record for MET-26-0457 shows the loading step was completed on
  2026-10-19 at 22:40. All in-process checks before loading passed.
- The equipment logbook for sieve S-201 has an entry from the previous shift:
  "screen found with a 15 mm tear during post-use inspection 2026-10-19 06:00".
- Maintenance work order WO-26-4512 shows the S-201 screen was replaced on
  2026-10-19 at 16:30, before the loading of this batch. The PM record shows the
  weekly screen integrity check for week 42 was marked "postponed".
- Environmental monitoring for Suite C on 2026-10-19 was within limits.
- Interview with the line operator (2026-10-20): "the loader was running with
  the sight glass cracked, I saw nothing unusual".
- The change control for the drum loader DL-03 (CC-26-0088) is still open; the
  new guarded sight glass is expected in November.

Please open the deviation. We suggest keeping the batch on hold until the
particles are identified by QC (FTIR) and the sieve/charger interface is
inspected. I have attached the packing records and the photo set to the
deviation folder.

